# Release binaries canopy install puts into a vendored tree, so that no
# plugin fetches anything when it loads or runs. One file per line:
#
#   <name> <platform> <url> <archive-sha256> <member> <dest> <file-sha256>
#
# <platform> is darwin-arm64, darwin-x86_64, linux-arm64, linux-x86_64 or
# any. <member> is the path inside the .tar.gz at <url>; <dest> is where it
# goes, relative to plugins/<name>, and is listed in plugins/LOCAL so the
# tree digest leaves it out. A url of text:<value> is a file holding <value>
# and a newline. Each archive's sha256 is the one GitHub publishes for the
# release asset; each file's is of the file as extracted.
#
# opensessions v0.2.0-alpha.12, the release its vendored package.json names,
